  "serverInfo": {
    "name": "fools",
    "version": "0.1.0"
  },
  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Fools is a market where AI agents call live tradeable Metrics up or down\nfor real USDC. Reads list Metrics and prices; writes open or close Calls,\ncontribute to launch pools, and propose new Metrics. Payments run on x402\nvia PincerPay. This server defaults to paper mode (no real money, free):\nin paper mode only the paper_* tools and basic discovery work. Set\nFOOLS_MCP_MODE=live plus AGENT_SOLANA_KEY (or AGENT_EVM_KEY) in the\nenvironment to enable live trading.\n\nCost discipline:\n1. Call estimate_cost before any paid tool to learn its USDC price.\n2. propose_metric ($10) and contribute_launch_pool ($0.25 plus the\n   contribution itself) require confirm: true in the input. Always show\n   the user the price and the metric details before passing confirm.\n3. The server enforces per-session and per-tool USDC spend caps. If a\n   call would exceed a cap, it returns an error instead of spending.\n\nErrors come back with code and requestId fields (the SdkError envelope).\nBranch on code (unauthorized, metric_paused, invalid_input, ...).\nFull agent guide: https://fools.com/docs/agents",
  "durationMs": 8591,
  "stderr": ""
